{
 "id": "E02",
 "title": "The Supercomputer India Couldn't Buy",
 "world": "network",
 "fps": 30,
 "seed": "s02",
 "passages": [
  {
   "id": "P01",
   "text": "You need a computer powerful enough for your research. You are told it is not available. What do you do next? Not a laptop. Not a machine for typing reports. A machine that could help model weather, materials, and enormous scientific problems.",
   "estSec": 23.3,
   "flag": "",
   "words": 42
  },
  {
   "id": "P02",
   "text": "In the nineteen eighties, access to advanced imported supercomputers became a serious obstacle for India. The easy response would have been to wait for permission. But a country that needs answers cannot always wait for somebody else's machine.",
   "estSec": 21.1,
   "flag": "",
   "words": 38
  },
  {
   "id": "P03",
   "text": "The Centre for Development of Advanced Computing, or C-DAC, was established in nineteen eighty-eight against the background of denied supercomputer imports. Its answer would become the PARAM family.",
   "estSec": 44.4,
   "flag": "",
   "words": 80
  },
  {
   "id": "P04",
   "text": "That is parallel computing. Instead of expecting one processor to perform every calculation, a supercomputer distributes work across many processors. Each handles a portion. Then the results are brought together.",
   "estSec": 48.9,
   "flag": "",
   "words": 88
  },
  {
   "id": "P05",
   "text": "And there is a third problem. Think of a relay race. A fast runner cannot finish the race if the baton is dropped. In parallel computing, software decides how work is divided, how tasks communicate, and when partial answers are combined. Poor coordination can erase the advantage of all that hardware.",
   "estSec": 28.3,
   "flag": "",
   "words": 51
  },
  {
   "id": "P06",
   "text": "This is why a supercomputer is not simply a room filled with computers. It is an agreement between hardware, networks, memory, software, cooling and people who understand the problems being solved.",
   "estSec": 41.1,
   "flag": "",
   "words": 74
  },
  {
   "id": "P07",
   "text": "Here is a fictional scenario. A weather model is divided among many processors. One processor finishes early, but another is still calculating. The whole system must manage that imbalance. If communication and scheduling are poor, adding more processors may barely improve the result. That is the hidden art behind the machine.",
   "estSec": 28.3,
   "flag": "FICTIONAL SCENARIO",
   "words": 51
  },
  {
   "id": "P08",
   "text": "Today's frontier is different. Supercomputing now depends on accelerators, high-speed networks, energy efficiency and software tuned to new architectures. Global supply chains still matter. Independence is a moving target.",
   "estSec": 32.2,
   "flag": "",
   "words": 58
  },
  {
   "id": "P09",
   "text": "The barrier was not defeated by pretending it did not exist. It was answered by learning how the entire system worked.",
   "estSec": 15.6,
   "flag": "",
   "words": 28
  }
 ],
